{"qid":"Q577867","names":["Kingdom of Poland"],"title":"Kingdom of Poland","endonym":null,"capsule":"The Kingdom of Poland emerged from the Piast duchy when Bolesław I the Brave received a royal crown from Holy Roman Emperor Otto III in 1000 and was formally crowned in 1025; the kingdom achieved continuous royal status from 1320 when Władysław I was crowned at Kraków. Under Casimir III the Great (r.1333–1370), the kingdom codified its law, established Kraków University (1364), and extended control eastward into Ruthenia. The dataset span closes in 1449 on the eve of the Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth's consolidation under the Jagiellonian dynasty, which linked Poland to Lithuania and eventually Bohemia and Hungary.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Core territory of the Piast and early Jagiellonian kingdom is well attested from chronicles, papal correspondence, and royal cadastres; eastern borderlands with Lithuania and Ruthenia are less precisely delimited in the geometries.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Britannica: Poland","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Poland"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Kingdom of Poland","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Poland"}],"britannica":null,"cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Kingdom of Poland","rulers":[{"qid":null,"name":"Mieszko I","nativeName":"Mieszko I","roman":"Mieszko I","start":962,"end":992,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Bolesław I the Brave","nativeName":"Bolesław I Chrobry","roman":"Bolesław I Chrobry","start":992,"end":1025,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Mieszko II Lambe